{#
    Overrides Sylius' own @SyliusShop/order/thank_you.html.twig (standard
    Symfony bundle-template-override mechanism - templates/bundles/<Bundle
    class name>/<path>, NOT a vendor-code edit).

    LOCATION MATTERS - DO NOT MOVE THIS INTO sulu-overlay/:
    this route is served by SYLIUS, so the override has to live in the
    Sylius app's own templates/ directory (the project root). It
    originally sat in sulu-overlay/templates/bundles/, which made
    make sulu-theme copy it into the Sulu app - where nothing ever reads
    it, leaving it silently ineffective (see FIXES.md No. 45).

    Why this exists: Adyen's own SuccessfulResponseProcessor redirects
    here after a completed payment (hard-coded route name
    "sylius_shop_order_thank_you", not configurable - see FIXES.md
    No. 33). Rather than let the customer briefly see Sylius' own,
    differently-styled confirmation page, this template immediately
    forwards to our own Sulu confirmation page instead - so this route
    only needs to be reachable, never actually seen.

    order.number confirmed available here directly from
    OrderController::thankYouAction() in Sylius core, which renders this
    template with ['order' => $order] - the same Order entity our own
    checkout already reads .number from elsewhere in this project.

    Meta-refresh instead of a Twig/PHP redirect: this template is reached
    via reverse_proxy from Caddy, and a plain HTML redirect here is the
    simplest mechanism that works regardless of how the response is
    proxied - no JavaScript dependency, no extra round trip through a
    redirect response Caddy would need to relay correctly.
#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="de">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url=/checkout/bestaetigung/{{ order.number }}">
    <title>Weiterleitung …</title>
</head>
<body>
    <p>
        Einen Moment bitte …
        <a href="/checkout/bestaetigung/{{ order.number }}">Weiter zur Bestätigung</a>
    </p>
</body>
</html>
